the three-month moving average ending in the month shown. The one-year change subtracts the same measure twelve months earlier; significance uses Statistics Canada's standard error of the year-over-year change.","Ottawa and Gatineau use the LFS's Ontario and Quebec parts of the Ottawa-Gatineau CMA."],"limitations":["The LFS is a sample survey; estimates for small metros are volatile and Statistics Canada rounds to one decimal. Levels and changes are not forecasts.","Rates describe all residents 15+, including students, retirees and people outside the labour force, and say little about opportunities for a specific occupation or for people who are not yet in Canada.","For Nunavut the published seasonally adjusted values equal the unadjusted values in every month since 2019 (and in about a third of months for the Northwest Territories), so the SA label is largely nominal there."],"sourceIds":["statcan-14-10-0459-01","statcan-14-10-0292-01","statcan-14-10-0462-01"],"relatedPlaceIds":["calgary","gatineau","kelowna","london","montreal","ottawa","sherbrooke","toronto","vancouver"],"computedAt":"2026-11-04T18:02:44+00:00"}